    </div>
    <div class="hx-sol-grid">
        <div class="hx-sol"><span class="hx-icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg></span><h3>The formatted disk that keeps talking</h3><p>A simple format does not remove data: it removes the index. Whoever receives the machine — leasing company, buyer or recipient — can recover files with free software.</p><span class="hx-cost">Real cost: an incident under the LGPD — Brazil's data protection law — with penalties of up to 2% of Brazilian turnover (capped at R$ 50 million), born from equipment that left 'clean'.</span></div>
        <div class="hx-sol"><span class="hx-icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="18"/><path d="M8 7h2M8 11h2M8 15h2M14 7h2M14 11h2M14 15h2M10 21v-3h4v3"/></svg></span><h3>The leasing return that takes your data with it</h3><p>The returned machine is refurbished and goes to the next organisation. Without recorded sanitisation, your contracts and spreadsheets travel in the package.</p><span class="hx-cost">Real cost: strategic data circulating outside your control — not even counted as a detectable breach.</span></div>
        <div class="hx-sol"><span class="hx-icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l10 18H2L12 3z"/><path d="M12 10v5M12 18h.01"/></svg></span><h3>The donation that becomes a headline</h3><p>Donating computers is excellent — until a piece of sensitive data turns up on the donated machine. The social gesture becomes a reputational crisis and a legal case.</p><span class="hx-cost">Real cost: the organisation's social project suspended and the brand associated with a breach — for the wrong reason.</span></div>
