    <div class="hx-head-split">
      <div><span class="hx-label">Frequently asked questions</span><h2>What IT, security and the DPO ask</h2></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hx-faq">
        <details><summary>What is the difference between sanitisation and formatting?</summary><p>Formatting removes the index of the files; the data stays on the disk and is recoverable with common tools. Sanitisation applies a documented method of logical removal to make the data unrecoverable — with a record of the process per media.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is the equipment still usable afterwards?</summary><p>Yes — that is the difference from physical destruction. Sanitised media stays functional, ready for leasing return, internal reuse or donation.</p></details>
        <details><summary>And if the media is damaged or encrypted?</summary><p>The assessment identifies media where sanitisation is not technically applicable. In those cases, we recommend physical destruction, to the same standard of record-keeping.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does the report identify each media?</summary><p>Yes, subject to scope: the media treated appears identified in the report, with the method applied — it is the format that audits and DPOs ask for.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do you also collect and dispose of the equipment?</summary><p>Yes. Sanitisation can be contracted on its own or integrated with collection, disposal and documentation for the batch — inventory, MTR and CDF where applicable.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can our head office verify the documentation from outside Brazil?</summary><p>Yes. The final destination certificate carries a QR code that any auditor, anywhere, can validate in seconds — the system itself confirms its authenticity, with no calls to Brazil and no translation needed. Every client also uses the Ecobraz evidence portal free of charge, with no contract: the records of each collection are organised under your company registration and can be exported to feed the compliance or ESG system your group already uses.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

